@startuml bidding-sequence
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam sequenceDividerFontStyle bold
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC

skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #42A5F5
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  FontStyle bold
}

skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #7E57C2
  BackgroundColor #EDE7F6
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #E0D68A
  FontSize 11
}

title Task_RFQ + Bid_Object Bidding Protocol\n(Paper §6.1: Task_RFQ broadcast + signed Bid_Objects)

actor "Buyer Agent" as Buyer
participant "Go Server\n(MCP / HTTP)" as Server
database "SQLite" as DB
participant "x402 Bazaar" as Bazaar
actor "Worker Agent A" as WorkerA
actor "Worker Agent B" as WorkerB
participant "Base L2\n(Contracts)" as Chain

== RFQ Broadcast ==

Buyer -> Server : create_rfq / POST /api/v1/rfqs\n(title, budget_min/max, deadline, requirements)
Server -> DB : INSERT rfq (status=open)
Server --> Buyer : rfq_id, status=open

note over Bazaar : Workers discover RFQs via\nBazaar /discovery/resources\nor GET /api/v1/rfqs?status=open

== Bid Submission ==

WorkerA -> Server : place_bid / POST /api/v1/rfqs/{id}/bids\n(amount=200, duration=3600)
Server -> DB : Validate: amount in [budget_min, budget_max],\nbidder != buyer, RFQ is open
Server -> DB : INSERT bid (status=pending)
Server --> WorkerA : bid_id, status=pending

WorkerB -> Server : place_bid / POST /api/v1/rfqs/{id}/bids\n(amount=300, duration=7200)
Server -> DB : INSERT bid (status=pending)
Server --> WorkerB : bid_id, status=pending

== Bid Evaluation ==

Buyer -> Server : list_bids / GET /api/v1/rfqs/{id}/bids
Server -> DB : SELECT bids WHERE rfq_id=?
Server --> Buyer : [bid_A(200), bid_B(300)]

note over Buyer : Evaluate bids:\ncost, reputation, capability\n(Paper §4.3: multi-objective optimization)

== Bid Acceptance → Escrow Formalization ==

Buyer -> Server : accept_bid / POST /api/v1/rfqs/{id}/accept\n(bid_id=bid_A)

group Atomic acceptance
  Server -> Chain : createEscrow(buyer, worker_A,\namount=200, verifier, arbitrator, deadline)
  Chain --> Server : tx_hash, escrow_address, escrow_id

  Server -> DB : INSERT task + escrow (status=created)
  Server -> DB : UPDATE bid_A: status=accepted, escrow_id=N
  Server -> DB : UPDATE rfq: status=closed
  Server -> DB : UPDATE bid_B: status=rejected
end

Server --> Buyer : escrow_id, escrow_address, tx_hash

note over WorkerB : Bid rejected;\nfree to bid on other RFQs

== Post-Acceptance: Standard Escrow Lifecycle ==

note over Buyer, Chain : Buyer funds escrow → Worker submits → Verifier approves → Settlement\n(See lifecycle-sequence diagram)

@enduml
